{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>On the tenth of this month, and they shall take for themselves.</b> It was the day of Shabbat, and because Israel performed in it the first commandment, such as taking the paschal lamb on the tenth, it is called Shabbat HaGadol." "<b>And they shall take for themselves, each man, a lamb.</b> Because the constellation of Aries was their object of worship, and on its account they worshipped flocks — 'you shall take your fear in your hand,' and they will have no ability to hold you back. And they shall take it in the month whose constellation is Aries, and it will not avail it." "<b>A lamb for a father's house.</b> Even if they are not from one family, but they are in one house — they may take for themselves a lamb." "<b>A lamb for a house.</b> To find their fear in each and every house."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:04.707092991Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}